    detect: 'Script: child_process exec/execSync (and spawn/execFile with shell: true) where the command contains `${…}` or concatenation, flagged more strongly when request data is involved; also Python os.system and subprocess with shell=True. Build scripts and tooling folders are skipped.',
    fix: 'Avoid the shell. Use execFile or spawn with an argument array (`execFile(\'convert\', [input, output])`), validate inputs against strict allowlists, and prefer a library over shelling out.',
