    why: 'Reflecting any origin with credentials lets any website make authenticated requests to your API and read the answers: cross-site data theft.',
    detect: 'Script: cors() with defaults or origin: \'*\', origin: true or callback(null, true), and Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * in code or provider header config. Reflection plus credentials = fail. With --url it also sends one GET with a probe Origin header to see whether it gets reflected.',
    fix: 'Allow an explicit list of your own origins (`cors({ origin: [\'https://app.example.com\'], credentials: true })`), never reflect arbitrary origins with credentials, and keep `*` only for truly public, unauthenticated, read-only endpoints.',
